                "choice_label": "E",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$20e^{-j\\pi/12}$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              }
            ],
            "correct_choice_labels": [
              "A"
            ],
            "correct_answer": "$20e^{j\\pi/12}$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Multiply the magnitudes to get $4\\cdot 5=20$. Then add the phase exponents: $j\\pi/4-j\\pi/6=j\\pi/12$, and the $\\omega$ terms cancel because $-j\\omega/3+j\\omega/3=0$. So $Y(j\\omega)=20e^{j\\pi/12}$.",
